-- title:
--   Chart rings localise with the base ring
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $F$ a field which is an $R$-algebra, and $R'$ a commutative ring which is an $R$-algebra and over which $F$ is an algebra, the two structures on $F$ being compatible (a scalar tower $R \to R' \to F$). Let $M \subseteq R$ be a submonoid such that $R'$ is a localisation of $R$ at $M$, and let $S \subseteq F$ be an arbitrary subset. For a base ring $B \in \{R, R'\}$ write $A_B(S)$ for the $B$-subalgebra `chartAlg B F S` of $F$ consisting of those $x \in F$ that are integral over the $B$-subalgebra of $F$ generated by $S$, i.e. the integral closure of $B[S]$ in $F$. Since $A_R(S) \subseteq A_{R'}(S)$, the inclusion ring homomorphism `chartBaseChange R F R' S` makes $A_{R'}(S)$ an $A_R(S)$-algebra; this is the algebra structure used in the conclusion. The assertion is that, for this structure, $A_{R'}(S)$ is a localisation of $A_R(S)$ at the image of $M$ under the structure map $R \to A_R(S)$: the images of elements of $M$ are units in $A_{R'}(S)$, every element of $A_{R'}(S)$ is such an image times the image of an element of $A_R(S)$, and the map $A_R(S) \to A_{R'}(S)$ has the expected kernel behaviour.
--
--   This is the statement that forming the integral closure of $B[S]$ in $F$ commutes with localising the base ring, specialised to the chart rings used to build the two-chart integral model of a curve. It is used in the construction of that model's base-change and pullback properties, among them [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.isPullback_chartFin`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.isPullback_chartFin) and the existence statements for pullback squares over a localised base.
-- source:
